  "name": null,
  "problem": "A particular shop sells chickens and turkeys. The weight of a chicken is normally distributed with a mean of $1.5\\,\\text{kg}$ and a standard deviation of $0.1\\,\\text{kg}.$ The weight of a turkey is normally distributed with a mean of $8\\,\\text{kg}$ and a standard deviation of $0.4\\,\\text{kg}.$ If a chicken and a turkey are randomly selected, what is the probability that $5$ times the weight of the chicken is greater than the turkey's weight? You may assume that the weights are independent. \n\n*Hint: A table of values of $Φ(z)$ for different values of $z$ is given below, where $Φ(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution. *\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.05\\,$ | $\\,0.06\\,$ | $\\,0.07\\,$ | $\\,0.08\\,$ | $\\,0.09\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,0.7\\,$ | $\\,0.7734\\,$ | $\\,0.7764\\,$ | $\\,0.7794\\,$ | $\\,0.7823\\,$ | $\\,0.7852\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.8\\,$ | $\\,0.8023\\,$ | $\\,0.8051\\,$ | $\\,0.8078\\,$ | $\\,0.8106\\,$ | $\\,0.8133\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.9\\,$ | $\\,0.8289\\,$ | $\\,0.8315\\,$ | $\\,0.8340\\,$ | $\\,0.8365\\,$ | $\\,0.8389\\,$ |",
  "worked_solution": "",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
